WEBVTT

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.860
So-phie-chan...

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.740
You're back.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.370
Your alarm's going off.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.870
Aren't you getting up?

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.910
I'm getting up.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.790
Just ten more minutes.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.670
Wow, she really does sleep in a coffin.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:32.800
Sakuya?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.840
Heya.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.390
Hinata's here, too?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.060
Thanks in advance!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.640
Thanks... for what?

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.530
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.530
<b>Interview with the Vampire</b>

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.540
Huh? I called you.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.620
Didn't you hear it?

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.870
You did?

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.000
Wait, come to think of it...

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.170
That's not the alarm.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.920
<b>Incoming Call
Akari</b>

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.920
Is that Akari? What does she want?

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.470
Hello?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.300
<i>Oh, sorry, were you asleep?</i>

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.430
It's fine.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.940
Sakuya-chan was saying she wants 
to cover you for her club.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.400
Cover me?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.440
Is it okay if we come now?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.900
<i>Okay, I'll get up and change.</i>

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.700
Then I'm coming, too!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.360
Was she sleeping just now?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.820
Seems so.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.290
Can I document how she sleeps, too?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.080
<i>What do you say, Sophie-chan?</i>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.410
I don't mind.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.710
So I should just keep sleeping?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.710
Then I'll get more sleep.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.090
I do remember that.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.970
<b>Was half asleep
 and totally forgot</b>

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.260
So what's this about covering me?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.180
What kind of club is this for?

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.270
I'm in an occult club for fun.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.560
I upload ghost stories and 
other strange stories,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.320
and since you're a vampire I know,
I thought I could maybe

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:37.820
do an article about you.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.190
I see.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.990
I'm representing the club.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.280
Wow, you're the representative?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.030
I'm still recruiting everyone else.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.660
Is it even a club if there's
 only one person in it?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.620
Yuu helps me out sometimes.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.500
Hey, Yuu-neechan?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.290
Yeah?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.260
How come you're not hanging 
out with Sakuya-neechan today?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.470
She has her club today.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.720
A club?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.300
Oh, that ghost thing.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.890
A while ago, I did some 
research at a temple that does

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.440
funerals for dolls, because they 
have a doll with growing hair.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.810
Want to see pictures of it?

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:15.810
I'm good.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.610
Not interested.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.360
I do, I do!

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.860
A doll with hair that keeps 
growing sounds so romantic.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.240
Right?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.280
The occult is romantic.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.660
I wonder if they'd let 
me have a doll like this.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.620
It would be so wonderful if I 
could put her in the living room.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.170
Please never do that.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.300
I'm going to change now, so why 
don't you wait in the living room?

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.260
Got it.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.590
We'll be waiting.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.560
Why don't I help you, Sophie-chan?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.560
No way.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.730
I can't trample all over 
Sakuya's expectations.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.860
It seems like she'll be putting it online, too.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.820
So this is what a vampire's 
living room looks like.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.740
It does look the part, kind of.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:11.580
Right?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.500
I thought the same thing 
the first time I saw it.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:17.880
Cosplay?!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.960
That's different.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.460
Shall we begin?

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.380
Wait a second! You don't usually dress like that!

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.010
That's true...

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:31.260
I was thinking maybe I should dress 
more like a vampire for the interview.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.560
It's fantastic!

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.680
You look just like the 
vampires in the movies!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.900
<i>She actually likes it.</i>

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.310
You look cute in a new outfit like this, too!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.320
<i>Akari, too?</i>

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.690
Even though she's here for an interview,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.450
you don't need to do anything 
special. Just be yourself.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.450
Is that how it works?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.740
It is!

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.370
I want to see you in your most natural state,

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.620
so just do what you always do.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.420
Do what I always do?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.880
Yes, and I'd like to take pictures and 
ask you a few things here and there.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.300
Sure.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.840
Do what I always do... Do what I always do...

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.470
So what are you doing now?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.100
I'm checking my email and looking at Twitter.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.810
Checking email and Twitter...

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.720
And now?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.690
I ordered some blood and anime figures online.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.610
I see.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.700
Maybe these pictures are too boring, though.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.530
Maybe I should lift a road roller, 
and you could take a picture of that.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.540
That's not an everyday thing for you!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.370
You don't have to do anything special!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.580
Okay...

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.630
But how come you're writing 
an article about a vampire?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.960
Because I watch a lot of vampire movies.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.010
I just love all those cool black clothes.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.260
Why do vampires wear black clothes, though?

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:58.930
Is it to further their dark image, 
or is there some other reason?

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.400
The reason?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.480
Yeah!

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.320
Because blood stains clothes easily,

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.860
so you want a color that 
makes it less noticeable.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.870
It's hard to get blood out.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.450
So that's why!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.780
I totally get it!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.790
I also avoid wearing white 
when I eat curry udon.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.540
That's the same thing?!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.000
In movies, vampires and 
werewolves are often depicted

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.710
as enemies or fighting each other.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.720
Is that true?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:37.640
Is not getting along with werewolves 
a thing for you, too?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.930
Werewolves are nothing but a superstition.

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.310
How absurd.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.690
<i>Can a vampire say that?</i>

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:45.940
Huh?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.940
My last question is for Akari-chan.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.530
How did you end up living with Sophie-chan?

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.790
Well... The first time I met her,
I thought she was so beautiful,

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.790
just like a doll!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.000
After that, we became friends.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.040
Heya, Sophie-chan!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.960
I came to visit you.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.050
She was living all alone in 
this big house and I thought

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.350
it looked pretty lonely.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:25.400
I thought maybe she wouldn't 
be lonely anymore if I moved in.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.320
And then I thought 
that if I moved in, I could

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.700
comb her silky silver hair every 
day and play dress-up with her.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.660
It started out nice and innocent, but then...

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.540
It's gotten pretty dark outside.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.330
It's the gloaming.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.870
The gloaming?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:49.000
It's the time when people are most 
likely to encounter a monster.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.170
Sophie! My computer came in yesterday, 
but it doesn't seem to be working right.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.010
Can you take a look?

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.010
One just encountered us.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.100
What... did you do, exactly?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.470
Just gave it a little chop.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:03.930
I see.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.900
I guess you being able to tell 
me what you did is progress.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.940
The computer is beyond help, though.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.400
Let me borrow yours for a bit.
I'm going to order a new one.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.150
Don't touch it! I'll order it.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.280
That's Ellie-chan.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.910
Come on, I just want to 
use it for a little bit.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.700
She's a vampire like Sophie-chan,

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.450
Why won't you let me use it real quick?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.790
and she recently woke up
 from a hundred-year slumber.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.130
That's why she still has a little 
difficulty with modern machines.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.170
"Little" doesn't even begin to describe it.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.630
Oh, I've never seen you before.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.010
This is my friend Sakuya-chan.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.090
It's nice to meet you!

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.050
My name's Ellie.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.180
You're so tiny and cute!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.970
S-Sakuya, hold on!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.980
She gets really mad when 
you treat her like a child.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.850
Oh! R-Really?

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:47.980
What should I do?

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.940
Stare...

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.700
Well, you're really cute, too!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.530
Huh?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.870
<i>She thinks they're birds of a feather...</i>

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.370
<b>Confidential</b>

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.040
So you're interested in vampires?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:05.580
Yeah!

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.420
Want to get your blood sucked by 
a vampire? For the experience.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.290
This might be a rare opportunity!

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.550
<i>How exciting.</i>

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.930
Your skin looks so delicious...

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.100
Just so you know, Ellie's bite really hurts.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.730
A-Actually, I'll pass.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.400
I can't handle needles, either.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:35.400
Darn it! Why'd you have to say that, Sophie?

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.570
Because it's the truth.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:45.660
Did you know that there are a lot 
of ghost stories about this area?

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.250
That's terrifying.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.660
When I moved here, it wasn't like that.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:53.720
<i>It's because there's a vampire 
walking around late at night!</i>

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:54.920
Ah!

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.010
Stop staring at nothing!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:06.210
Not that I'm scared, but there's 
really nothing there, right?

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.010
There's nothing there.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:12.190
I was just looking in the
hope of seeing something.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.280
<b>Confidential</b>

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:19.030
You know, I run the occult club,

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.910
but I've never seen a ghost or a UFO before.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.710
You haven't?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:31.080
But you know, I love that just the thought of
 something extraordinary being out there

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.170
makes me excited.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:41.120
That's why I'm really happy that I got 
to meet and talk to real vampires!

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.380
One of my dreams actually came true.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.950
<i>I hope us being this kind of vampire 
didn't destroy her dreams.</i>

00:11:58.940 --> 00:11:59.950
Shoot.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:03.380
I ended up binge-watching 
this entire anime series.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.130
Now it's almost noon.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.040
I really need to get to bed.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.360
Sophie!

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.230
Ellie, what are you doing here?

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.820
Is it an emergency?

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:15.600
We're going out!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.340
Do you have any idea what time it is?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.300
It's time for vampires to be asleep.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.890
But I don't feel sleepy.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:26.630
So where are you going at this hour?

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.540
I'm going to buy clothes!

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.850
Hinata told me about this one store.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.980
We'd be too rushed if we 
went there after sundown.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.050
Just buy everything online.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.930
Going out during the day is dangerous.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.260
But you can't see the fine details 
if you don't go in person!

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.900
Well, I'm out. I'm going to bed.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.450
You can't!

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.990
All you've got in your closet is 
old stuff that all looks the same!

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:52.890
Just how many centuries old <i>is</i> this?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.930
Go out and buy something 
from <i>this</i> century!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:57.700
Sorry I kept you waiting!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:01.430
I was just thinking I wanted 
to go buy some summer clothes.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.380
I called Hinata, too.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.000
She's meeting us at the station.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.680
Oh, I forgot my sunscreen.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.130
What's that?

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:12.600
You put it on your skin, and then 
it won't get burned by the sun.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:17.000
Do you think vampires can use that, too?

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.850
I'm not sure...

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:21.080
It doesn't work on vampires.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:27.730
Even if it did, you might 
end up like Earless Houichi.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.860
I forgot to cover my ears!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:31.750
What? That sounds terrifying.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.640
Time to go!

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.090
Hey, Ellie...

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.020
The sun is really strong this time of year.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.640
Are you okay? Should we 
try again on a cloudy day?

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:55.890
I'm fine!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.630
I can handle this if it
 means getting cute clothes!

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.240
Let's take a short break.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.070
Y-Yeah...

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.320
All right, let's go.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.470
We've made good progress.

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:17.400
Yeah. That was probably
 at least a hundred meters.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:24.080
They're late. I wonder if everything's okay...

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.480
Hinata-chan!

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.930
Come on, you two, you've almost made it.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:33.900
Sorry for the wait.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.250
Are you okay?!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.540
I guess there are no open seats.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:48.010
Hey, Akari. There's nothing else free,
so why don't they just use these?

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:49.900
I'll do that.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.360
Wait, Ellie... This is...

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:56.080
Please offer these seats to others

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:56.080
Well, you're probably <i>old</i> enough...

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.530
Don't treat us like senior citizens.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.040
What are you, then?

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.360
It's so nice that there's a roof.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.680
We made it somehow.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.060
There really are a lot of clothes here.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:14.920
Indeed.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.470
There are a lot of different stores here.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:20.370
We can pick whatever we want!

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.510
There's too much to choose from, though.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.430
Let's just take our time looking around, then.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.620
This looks perfect.

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.090
I like this one.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.790
I think I'll get this.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.170
You all picked stuff that's just 
like what you always wear!

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.010
Now that you mention it...

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.930
Oh, so did I!

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:01.700
I always end up picking 
the same kinds of things.

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.120
Same here.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.150
True, true.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.900
I know! Since we're all here together,

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.610
how about we pick out clothes for each other?

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:11.690
That sounds good!

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.690
We might end up wearing 
things we don't usually wear.

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:21.300
Sophie-chan, how about this 
rococo-style dress?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.380
Oh, that brings back memories.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:24.760
Those used to be popular.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.340
Where did you even find that thing?

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.540
How about we look at some more places?

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:32.910
Agreed!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.820
Akari, you're into stuff like this, right?

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.130
Don't you want to try it on?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:44.520
I like looking at it, but I prefer to wear
 things that are a bit more subdued.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.020
How about black?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:46.720
Huh?

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.310
I like that it's not so bright during the day.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:52.130
And stains don't stand out 
when you get covered in blood.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.380
I highly recommend it!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:56.130
Uh, Akari doesn't get covered in blood...

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.410
Black, huh?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.080
I haven't worn much black before.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:05.560
<i>If I match Sophie-chan and Ellie-chan, 
we might look like sisters.</i>

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:12.380
Yes, I'll take it!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:14.360
Akari's covered in blood!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:20.580
I'd like you to find something modern,
from the 21st century.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.100
Well, I look good in anything, but you know.

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.960
Something that would look good on Ellie...

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.890
Mom, I want that!

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.040
Oh, that's so cute.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.340
What do you think?

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:34.820
It suits you too well.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.920
You were just thinking something rude.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:40.240
You got me there.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:41.850
Grr...

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.450
I'm sorry, Ellie! Don't be so mad!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.910
I promise I'll pick something properly now.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.680
Well, I'm not expecting much from you.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.350
All right, I'll show you that 
I can pick something good!

00:17:57.770 --> 00:18:02.590
Hmm... That being said, if I were
 to pick something, this would be it.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:06.400
I'm sorry, Ellie. This isn't your style, huh?

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:09.000
I'll do you a favor and go with this.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.910
If that's the case, we should 
match it with this parka and—

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.730
Oh, but this shirt and 
these shorts are good, too!

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.580
Wouldn't this look good on Hinata?

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.680
That's so cute!

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:26.820
Really?

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:28.910
Is this payback for before?

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:31.540
I don't look good in skirts.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.760
That's not true. Just try it on.

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:42.090
D-Does it look weird?

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.350
It's great!

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.950
Take a look in the mirror!

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.880
I look like a girl.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.650
You <i>are</i> a girl.

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:02.450
It'll take some courage to put this on.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:06.120
It's fine. Just trust my fashion sense.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.100
Sophie-chan is next, then.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:09.380
Right.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.380
What should we try?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.090
Casual?

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.960
Or sporty?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.380
Those clothes are cute, too.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.010
It's so hard to pick!

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.930
Please go easy on me.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:34.470
I'm ready.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.990
How is it? Do you like what I picked?

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.690
You usually wear black, but I 
thought white could be nice, too.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:46.580
I think I should go for something 
that's more like what I usually wear.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:50.650
Sophie-chan, look here for a second.

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:56.010
Yup, it looks great on you!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.320
Really? Thanks.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.310
I'll get this, then.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.810
Great!

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.130
Okay, time to change back.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.280
Huh?

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:17.610
Where are the clothes I was just wearing?

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:18.980
Excuse me.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.360
She wants to keep wearing 
the outfit she just tried on.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.780
Could you put her other 
clothes in a bag, please?

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.300
Of course. Thank you very much.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.450
When did she...

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.390
If possible, please vacuum pack them.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.370
Pardon me?

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.390
I'm kinda hungry.

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:41.790
How about we get crêpes?

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:46.030
The azuki strawberry and 
the custard ones look good!

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.300
The chocolate banana one looks yummy, too!

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.340
They all look so good, I can't decide!

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.770
Humans really love their sugar, huh?

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.910
That's so charming.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.230
I'm hungry, too.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:03.320
That graceful-looking girl and 
that refreshing-looking girl

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.940
both look delicious!

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:08.430
When there are so many of them,
 it's hard to decide.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:11.020
Hey, don't say stuff like that.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:23.030
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:23.030
<b>Summer Break Spent with a Vampire</b>

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:47.050
It was so satisfying to buy all those things.

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:49.590
I usually buy everything online,

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:53.310
but going shopping with friends 
once in a while is nice, too.

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:57.070
Once summer break starts, I want 
to go out in the new things we got!

00:22:57.070 --> 00:22:57.890
Sounds good!

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:59.230
Summer break?

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:01.350
I guess it's already that time of year.

00:23:02.580 --> 00:23:04.760
Summer break, huh?

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:09.470
I know! Why don't we go watch fireflies?

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:11.500
At night, you guys can move around easier.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:13.150
Fireflies? That sounds good.

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:14.550
How about we go now?

00:23:14.550 --> 00:23:15.330
Now?!

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:18.660
Maybe we can see some if 
we go up in the mountains?

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:22.700
What? But I'm already tired from 
all the walking we did today.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:24.100
Sophie, you're fine, right?

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:25.810
Let's go! Come on!

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:27.180
I'm going home to sleep.

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:30.340
Hey, wait up!

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:34.310
They're so lively once the sun goes down.

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:36.570
Do they just have infinite energy?

00:23:36.570 --> 00:23:39.180
Sophie! Wait up!
